{
  "schema": "orca.head_envelope.v1",
  "id": "bambu-a1-mini",
  "name": "Bambu Lab A1 mini (stock hotend and segmented ducts)",
  "provenance": "Floor: BambuStudio A1 / A1 mini machine presets set nozzle_height = 4.76 mm, the height below which Bambu's own clearance model has nothing but the nozzle, at most 4 mm across (MAX_OUTER_NOZZLE_DIAMETER): https://github.com/bambulab/BambuStudio/tree/47a13eeb1d9af65ef2371e361c856e21d4f6ca72/resources/profiles/BBL/machine . Sock and duct outlets start there. Community report of the A1 mini part cooler about 6.5 mm above the bed while printing (https://forum.bambulab.com/t/spacing-needed-when-using-by-object-printing-is-too-conservative/99336) agrees within the duct's slope; 4.76 is kept as the lower, published bound. Nozzle: 0.6 mm land and 35-degree half-angle cone of the Bambu hotend CAD (https://www.printables.com/model/533213 Hotend.STEP, X1/P1; the A1 hotend is the same nozzle family, both 47.3 mm long per Bambu's store listings), to the 4 mm envelope at Z=2.48, then a 4 mm cylinder to Z=4.76. Sock: lower skirt radius 4.5 to Z=6.5, then half-widths 9/7 enclosing the ceramic heater to Z=24. Ducts, from OEM toolhead photos (https://wiki.bambulab.com/en/a1-mini/maintenance/toolhead , front image /n1/a1-mini-print-head/toolhead.jpg at 0.317 mm/pixel, 52 mm duct width from https://www.printables.com/model/685475): outlets X=+-8..24, Y=+-8; outer walls X=+-24..26 from Z=6; risers X=+-8..26, Y=+-15 from Z=9; cover Z=23. Shared toolhead: https://wiki.bambulab.com/en/a1/manual/faq . BambuStudio A1 / A1 mini gantry underside 25 mm, farther edge 56.5 mm: symmetric Y span +-56.5, infinite X. Body axial/lateral margins 0.3 mm. Nozzle-tip frame +X right, +Y rear, +Z up, mm. Derived 2026-10-12; calibrated=false. A1 mini check (2026-10-17): the toolhead above the carriage is the A1-series part set, so every body box stays the A1's. The part cooling fan and its duct are one part for both printers (Bambu FAF006 'Part Cooling Fan (on Tool Head) - A1 mini, A1': https://www.3djake.com/bambu-lab/part-cooling-fan-on-tool-head , https://www.3dprintergear.com.au/bambu-lab-part-cooling-fan-on-tool-head-compatible ); the hotend is the 'A1 series' hotend ( https://eu.store.bambulab.com/en-gr/products/bambu-hotend-a1-series ); BambuStudio's A1 and A1 mini presets carry the same nozzle_height 4.76, extruder_clearance_height_to_rod 25, extruder_clearance_dist_to_rod 56.5 and extruder_clearance_max_radius 73 ( https://github.com/bambulab/BambuStudio/blob/master/resources/profiles/BBL/machine/Bambu%20Lab%20A1%20mini%200.4%20nozzle.json ). What differs is the X axis: the A1 mini's 'X-Axis Assembly - A1 mini' (FAC014, https://us.store.bambulab.com/products/x-axis-assembly-a1-mini ) is a cantilevered arm off the single left Z column. The arm is fixed in X and spans the whole 180 mm plate (the head reaches X 187 for the G39 check), so the gantry stays infinite in X; the community A1 mini model (https://www.printables.com/model/685475) puts the arm's underside about 40 mm above the tip and 34 mm deep in Y, inside Bambu's published 25 mm / +-56.5 mm, which is kept as the bound. The purge chute (X -13.5), wiper (X -30) and steel strip (Y 185) lie off the 180 x 180 plate and need no head or bed exclusion.",
